👻👻👻👻👻 FORMS AND HTTP POST 
!!! Adding a NEW NOTE IS DONE !!! 
trying to add something onto the server is a POST request 
The browser will send a POST request to the server with the data in the request body. 
<!-- WE OPEN THE DEVELOPER TOOL'S NETWORK TAB -->

SUBMITTING THE FORM CAUSES NO FEW THAN 5 HTTP requests, THE FIRST ONE IS THE FORM submit event.

http post request -  so the network tab shows the data submitted with the form:
  the data is sent as a PAYLOAD 

  THE CODE ON THE SERVER 

  app.post('/new_note', (req, res) => {
  notes.push({
    content: req.body.note,
    date: new Date(),
  })

  return res.redirect('/notes')
})

THE NEW DATA ADDED IS SENT AS THE BODY OF THE POST REQUEST 
THE SERVER CAN ACCESS THE DATA BY ACCESSING the req.body field of the request object req. 
so the server creates a new note object, and adds it to an array called notes.

notes.push({
  content: req.body.note,
  date: new Date(),
})


